HorizonDroid
===========

Getting started
---------------

To get started with Android/HorizonDroid, you'll need to get familiar with [Source Control Tools](https://source.android.com/setup/develop).

To initialize your local repository using the LineageOS trees, use a command like this:
```
repo init -u https://github.com/HorizonV2/android.git -b lineage-22.2 --git-lfs
```
or use this to save ur storage:
```
repo init -u https://github.com/HorizonV2/android.git -b lineage-22.2 --git-lfs --depth=1
```
Then to sync up:
```
repo sync
```
HorizonDroid Flags:
```
# Maintainer username
HORIZON_MAINTAINER := Rve

# Face Unlock
TARGET_FACE_UNLOCK_SUPPORTED := true

# Gapps flags
WITH_GMS := true
WITH_GMS_VARIANT := pico/core
```
Setup environment:
```
. build/envsetup.sh
```
Generate keys command:
```
hk -s
```
Lunch options:
```
lunch lineage_<device>-bp1a-<buildtype>
```
Build command:
```
mka horizon -j$(nproc --all)
```
